{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-19025","model_call":45,"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"western union internal memo\" \"telephone\" (+ \"too many shortcomings\" \"no value\" \"seriously considered\"))"},"record":{"query":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"western union internal memo\" \"telephone\" (+ \"too many shortcomings\" \"no value\" \"seriously considered\"))"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_49_1339911292#12_2782355991","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q1776","rank":1,"snippet":"Quality Mangement Stress Management Lesson Learned In Conclusion \" , \"segment\": \"Change Management; Quality Management; Stress management. Leadership Path In the presentation, “Mission Possible: Effectively Managing a Crashed and Fastracked Shorten Interval Project” examples are given of project experiences that co-relate to each of the subcategories below on the Leadership Path and the Project Management Path. For the purposes of this paper, a brief highlight of the topic will be given with further elaboration to be given with examples a the conference presentation. Vision Behind every good project, a great leader should be found. Lack of leadership vision can have detrimental effects on a project and opportunities could be lost. Consider this statement from the <cover>Western Union Internal Memo 1876, “ The ‘telephone’ has too many shortcomings </cover>to be seriously considered as a means of communication. The device is inherently of no value to us” (Western Union Internal memo 1876, 2005).\" , \"start_char\": 6937.000000 , \"title\": \"Managing Crashed & Fastracked Shorten Interval Project\" , \"url\": \"https://www.pmi.org/learning/library/managing-crashed-fastracked-shorten-interval-project-7603\" }","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_49_1339911292#12_2782355991","rank":1,"relevance":2}]},"time":155},"model_calls":45,"document_judgments":36,"relevance_3":11,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
